  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Max Hyper Market India Private Limited vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 14 July, 2023 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh Bench: N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.Nos.21076 & In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 14.07.2023 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.Nos.21076 & 21080 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.Nos.13744 &13746 of 2022 1.Max Hyper Market India Private Limited (Spar Hyper Market) 83, Arcot Road, Vadapalani, Chennai - 600 026. represented by its Manager, Mr.Jai Shankar 2.Mr.Manikanda Prabhu (Nominee), S/o.Pongaliappan 3.Vivek Jothimani ... Petitioners in both Crl.O.Ps. -Vs- 1.Government of Tamil Nadu, Food and Safety Officer, No.545, Vadapalani Area, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drugs Department, O/o. Designated Officers Office, Chennai District, No.33, West Jones Road, Saidapet, Chennai - 600 015. 2.Sudhir Kumar S/o.Rajendra Varma 3.Saraswathi W/o.Y.Selvam ...Respondents in both Crl.O.Ps. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Max Hyper Market India Private Limited vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 14 July, 2023",
    "facts": "2. These petitions have been filed to quash the proceedings in C.C.Nos.97 & 98 of 2020 on the file of XVII Metropolitan Magistrate Court, Saidapet, Chennai. 3. The first respondent has enquired the criminal complaint against the petitioners for offences u/s.52 and 59(1) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 [for brevity 'the FSS Act']. 4.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel further submitted that the only reason that has been given for the delay was that there was some administrative delay and therefore, the report was given beyond the time stipulated u/s.42(2) of the FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel further submitted that the only reason that has been given for the delay was that there was some administrative delay and therefore, the report was given beyond the time stipulated u/s.42(2) of the FSS Act.",
